00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:09.300
expectations for most of us, especially when&nbsp;
it comes to life's most pressing questions.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:16.020
Why did God let this happen?
Why doesn't He answer my prayer?&nbsp;

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:21.120
What's His plan for my life?
We get frustrated and discouraged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:27.120
when we don't receive immediate answers.
Now, I'm not preaching to you guys because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:35.100
sometimes I'm guilty of this as well. Because&nbsp;
I don't follow God's will, I want to follow my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.700
own will and I want things to get done.
I want God to answer my prayers and I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.500
want it done my way.
And that's not right.&nbsp;

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.880
We should follow God's way all the time.
We should follow the example of Jesus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:49.740
when He prayed.
Not my will be done, but yours be done.&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.960
And Jesus said if you want to follow&nbsp;
me, then you need to deny yourself.&nbsp;

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.100
Pick up your cross and follow Jesus.
If you don't do that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.480
then you cannot follow Christ.
You cannot be a disciple and I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:08.100
say here we get frustrated and discouraged when&nbsp;
we don't receive immediate answers and that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.100
because we're acting in the flesh.
We want immediate answers.&nbsp;

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.340
We want our will instead&nbsp;
of focusing on God's will.&nbsp;

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:23.340
But look at 2 Timothy 3:16 to 17 which&nbsp;
describes the process of spiritual maturity.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:34.200
Teaching - rebuke - correction and training&nbsp;
- these things require time and effort.&nbsp;

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:40.140
It's not things that will happen immediately.
It requires time and effort.&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:46.200
They call for patience and diligence.
And they show us important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:52.260
truths about God and His Word.
First, God wants us to rely on Him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.660
not on ourselves.
On Him.&nbsp;

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.560
When Moses led the people of&nbsp;
Israel to the promised land,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:06.660
God provided just enough manna every&nbsp;
morning to sustain them for that day.&nbsp;

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:14.400
God wants us as His people to&nbsp;
come to Him daily for our needs.&nbsp;

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:19.920
He breathed out scripture because He&nbsp;
wants us to turn to His word every day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:24.960
for guidance and wisdom.
This is so important.&nbsp;

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:30.300
We live in a day and age where a lot&nbsp;
of people move away from God's word&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:36.780
and listen to preachers who preach to&nbsp;
itching ears - to false preachers - and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:39.240
they don't know God's Word.
When I ask a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.640
Christians - do you know the Bible?
Have you read it at least once?&nbsp;

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:44.880
They say no, even though they've&nbsp;
been Christians for years.&nbsp;

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.760
But Jesus says that if you love&nbsp;
me, you obey my commandments.&nbsp;

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.520
But how can you do that if&nbsp;
you don't know His word?&nbsp;

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.060
You can't.
You see, if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:05.340
want to become spiritually stronger you need to&nbsp;
go to the cross first and then to God's Word.&nbsp;

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.380
[
Hebrews 4:12]

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.680
This is where you get the difference between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:25.260
your soul life - your fleshly&nbsp;
nature - and the spiritual nature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:32.040
where you can become stronger by reading His word.
To read it, write it on your heart and to live it.&nbsp;

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.340
Not just to be hearers of&nbsp;
the Word, but to be doers.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:43.500
Second - the harder we search for something,&nbsp;
the more valuable it becomes to us.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:47.880
Proverbs 2 compares the wisdom&nbsp;
of God's Word to a treasure.&nbsp;

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:52.860
Like all good treasures,&nbsp;
it's not easily discovered.&nbsp;

00:05:52.860 --> 00:06:00.060
We must commit to searching the scriptures daily.
That's like the good Bereans, right?&nbsp;

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:03.600
Who searched the scriptures daily&nbsp;
to see if these things were so.&nbsp;

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:09.540
We have to dig - sift - and dig some more.
The harder we work to discover God's wisdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:13.260
the more we appreciate it.
When we find.&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:23.160
You know, my dad was a wonderful man.
I was blessed by God to give me my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:26.880
dad because he was a preacher.
But he lived the way he preached.&nbsp;

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:34.920
And all the sermons I heard from him -&nbsp;
the Bible studies together as a family -&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:40.440
all the things I learned from him -&nbsp;
they were like seeds put in my heart.&nbsp;

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:45.660
And now when I'm older I start to understand it.
Because it starts to to grow into plants.&nbsp;

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:50.700
Into a beautiful garden.
And this is so true.&nbsp;

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:55.860
The harder we work to discover God's wisdom,&nbsp;
the more we appreciate it when we find it.&nbsp;

00:06:55.860 --> 00:07:00.300
So now I start to understand things&nbsp;
that I couldn't understand before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:06.420
because I wasn't spiritually there yet.
But now a lot of the things that my dad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.720
said - because he was a spiritual&nbsp;
man - a mature Christian - he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:14.460
understood a lot of things that I don't.
But now I'm starting to understand more and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:20.220
more and it becomes more special to me now.
I appreciate it a lot more.&nbsp;

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.020
Third - spiritual maturity&nbsp;
is rarely what we imagine.&nbsp;

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:29.820
Our quest for God's wisdom is&nbsp;
often tied to a specific situation.&nbsp;

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:36.720
We want to know how to deal with a pressing&nbsp;
problem or receive guidance in making a decision.&nbsp;

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:43.620
Now, listen carefully.
But God has something much bigger in mind.&nbsp;

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:46.620
His ways are not our ways.&nbsp;

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:55.740
He wants to make us capable and equipped for&nbsp;
every good work, not just for this thing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:58.200
you have to take care of.
For every good work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:03.240
so He gives us more than we ask for.
Because He knows what we need.&nbsp;

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:08.100
He shows us perspectives we&nbsp;
could never see on our own.&nbsp;

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.060
In 2 Corinthians 12: 7 to 8,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:16.920
Paul said he prayed three times for God&nbsp;
to take away the thorn in his flesh.&nbsp;

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:23.460
Paul likely believed he could be a more effective&nbsp;
Christian minister without his affliction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:30.780
but God helped him see that his physical weakness&nbsp;
actually made him a more effective minister.&nbsp;

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:37.860
This is amazing because it shows us that&nbsp;
what we think is best for us is usually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:40.920
not what's best for us.
God, who is perfect.&nbsp;

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.340
We are not perfect.
God who is perfect, who's not even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.980
controlled by time, space, or matter.
He lives outside of it.&nbsp;

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:48.900
Because He created it.
He can see the future.&nbsp;

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:54.240
He knows what's best for you.
He knows exactly what we need.&nbsp;

00:08:54.240 --> 00:09:00.780
All we need to do is to fully trust&nbsp;
Him - not in ourselves - but in God.&nbsp;

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:05.340
Knowing - trusting - that He&nbsp;
knows what is best for us.&nbsp;

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:10.680
Fourth - God's timing is perfect.&nbsp;

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.340
This is something that you&nbsp;
will always need to remember.&nbsp;

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:21.960
He reveals His truths when we need them, and&nbsp;
when we are ready to understand and apply them.&nbsp;

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:25.860
This is so important.
We may read a certain Bible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:32.760
passage the same way 10 times in a row.
But as time passes, we grow in our faith.

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:40.500
When we are ready, God may reveal&nbsp;
a piece of truth in the passage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:45.540
that we have never noticed before.
That's how we grow.&nbsp;

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:50.160
I talked about this just a little bit earlier on.
The example that I use with my dad.&nbsp;

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:53.580
Certain things that he talked about -&nbsp;
scripture - that I didn't understand but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:58.800
now as I'm slowly maturing into a mature&nbsp;
Christian, I'm starting to understand it.&nbsp;

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:03.300
And let me tell you there's still&nbsp;
so much more that I don't know.&nbsp;

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:10.140
You know, walking on this road of&nbsp;
sanctification with God is like a gold mine.&nbsp;

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:14.700
You know, you just see there's a gold mine.
And you're here at the beginning, and you start to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:21.480
see the gold - but then when you look inside, you&nbsp;
see, man, there are tunnels leading everywhere.&nbsp;

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:25.260
And there's not just gold - there's diamonds.
So oh man, it just doesn't stop.&nbsp;

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:30.000
And that is it.
You will never stop to grow spiritually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:36.060
but while you are on this road of sanctification&nbsp;
you need to understand that God's timing is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:41.700
perfect and that you cannot force God to do&nbsp;
certain things when you are not ready for it yet.&nbsp;

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:44.160
Let's continue.&nbsp;

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:50.160
We plant the seeds by spending&nbsp;
time in prayer and in God's word.&nbsp;

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:57.840
But ultimately, God determines our right&nbsp;
of spiritual maturity when we abide in Him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:05.100
John 15 verse 4, right?
Abide in me - without me you can do nothing.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:14.220
You know, the older I get the&nbsp;
more precious this becomes to me.&nbsp;

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:18.600
Jesus, you know you can take the whole&nbsp;
world, but just keep giving me Jesus.&nbsp;

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:19.920
That's all I need.&nbsp;

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:25.260
I just want to abide in Him,&nbsp;
know him more deeper, fuller.&nbsp;

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:29.520
Jesus.
Always - only - Jesus.&nbsp;

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:34.260
Everything else this world - the things&nbsp;
of this world - it will pass away.&nbsp;

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:43.920
All that matters is your relationship with Jesus.
And I can't wait for that day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:51.120
when I will stand in front of Him.
Seeing His face, talking to Him, oh man.

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:57.720
I can talk about this the&nbsp;
whole day, but let's continue.&nbsp;

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:06.240
Now, this is the Bible study of Day 14.
We just finished it.&nbsp;

